💡 Docker Command Cheat Sheet

🔴Core Workflow:
→ docker version — Show Docker version information
→ docker pull [image] — Download image from registry
→ docker run [options] [image] — Create and start a container
→ docker ps — List running containers
→ docker ps -a — List all containers (including stopped)
→ docker stop [container] — Stop a running container
→ docker rm [container] — Remove a container

🔴Images & Registries:
→ docker images — List local images
→ docker rmi [image] — Remove an image
→ docker tag [image] [name:tag] — Tag an image for push
→ docker push [name:tag] — Push tagged image to registry

🔴Working with Containers:
→ docker exec -it [container] [command] — Run a command in a running container
→ docker logs [container] — Fetch logs from a container
→ docker inspect [container] — View detailed information for a container
→ docker cp [container]:[path] [local_path] — Copy files from container
→ docker attach [container] — Attach to a running container

🔴Volumes & Networking:
→ docker volume create [name] — Create a volume
→ docker volume ls — List volumes
→ docker volume rm [name] — Remove volume
→ docker network create [name] — Create network
→ docker network ls — List networks
→ docker network rm [name] — Remove network
→ docker run –-network [network] … — Run container on specific network
→ docker run -v [host_path]:[container_path] … — Mount volume

🔴Clean Up & Maintenance:
→ docker system prune — Remove all unused data (containers, networks, images)
→ docker container prune — Remove all stopped containers
→ docker image prune — Remove unused images
→ docker volume prune — Remove unused volumes

🔴Advanced Tools:
→ docker-compose up — Start services defined in docker-compose.yml
→ docker-compose down — Stop and remove services, networks, volumes
→ docker build -t [name:tag] [path] — Build image from Dockerfile
→ docker swarm init — Initialize Docker Swarm mode
→ docker service create — Create a new service in swarm
→ docker stack deploy -c [compose-file] [stack-name] — Deploy stack

🔴Configuration & Info:
→ docker info — Display system-wide information
→ docker version — Show version of client & server
→ docker inspect [resource] — Detailed info for container/image/volume
→ docker logs [container] — Fetch logs
→ docker stats — Display resource usage statistics
